WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.360
When Clara's father stepped onto the ground in front of Grandfather's hut, two girls walked toward him.

2
00:00:07.361 --> 00:00:16.233
Leaning on a smaller girl, whose eyes were dancing with joy, was a tall girl with fair hair and pink cheeks.

3
00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:21.974
She reminded Herr Sesemann of his late wife, and he almost thought he was dreaming.

4
00:00:21.975 --> 00:00:24.158
"Don't you know me, Papa?"

5
00:00:24.159 --> 00:00:28.210
called Clara, her face beaming with happiness.

6
00:00:28.211 --> 00:00:30.681
He stared at the two children.

7
00:00:30.682 --> 00:00:34.469
All at once, tears streamed from his eyes.

8
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.719
He ran to Clara and clasped her in his arms.

9
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.787
He stepped back to look at her again.

10
00:00:41.788 --> 00:00:43.772
"Are you my little Clara?

11
00:00:43.773 --> 00:00:49.192
Are you really my Clara?" he kept saying over and over.

12
00:00:49.193 --> 00:00:52.092
Heidi's heart beat with gladness.

13
00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:58.158
Herr Sesemann had always been good to her, and she was thrilled to see him so happy.

14
00:00:58.159 --> 00:01:05.762
Grandmamma introduced Herr Sesemann to Grandfather, and everyone settled down at Grandfather's table to talk.

15
00:01:05.763 --> 00:01:11.213
After a few moments, they heard a rustling noise from behind the goats' shed.

16
00:01:11.214 --> 00:01:16.133
"I think someone is hiding there," said Grandfather.

17
00:01:16.134 --> 00:01:19.123
Everyone looked; it was Peter.

18
00:01:19.124 --> 00:01:24.182
When Herr Sesemann saw Peter peek out from his hiding place, he called to him,

19
00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:27.320
"Come out, boy. Don't be afraid."

20
00:01:27.321 --> 00:01:30.073
Peter was scared stiff.

21
00:01:30.074 --> 00:01:36.724
He knew everyone was watching, so he screwed up his courage and came forward.

22
00:01:36.725 --> 00:01:43.683
"It was I. I broke it to pieces, and no one can put it together again," he exclaimed.

23
00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:48.094
Confused, Grandmamma and Herr Sesemann looked at each other.

24
00:01:48.095 --> 00:01:52.817
"Is that poor boy out of his mind?" asked Herr Sesemann.

25
00:01:52.818 --> 00:01:56.559
"Not in the least," said Grandfather.

26
00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:05.824
"It turns out that he was the wind that sent Clara's wheelchair down the mountain, and he is expecting his well-deserved punishment."

27
00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.790
But nobody wanted to punish Peter.

28
00:02:08.791 --> 00:02:14.519
Grandmamma thought he looked like a nice boy who had acted

29
00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:24.129
recklessly. Peter explained everything to her, including how he had been jealous of Heidi for having so many visitors and how he had missed seeing

30
00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:29.674
her. "You are a good boy to tell us," said Grandmamma, with a

31
00:02:29.675 --> 00:02:34.916
smile. "Now I will give you a gift for being

32
00:02:34.917 --> 00:02:37.974
truthful." Peter could hardly believe his

33
00:02:37.975 --> 00:02:42.534
ears. After careful thought, he shyly asked for a

34
00:02:42.535 --> 00:02:47.102
penny. Grandmamma laughed, opening her

35
00:02:47.103 --> 00:02:54.957
purse. "I will give you enough pennies to have a penny a week for a whole year!" she

36
00:02:54.958 --> 00:03:00.078
declared. After watching this scene, Herr Sesemann put his hand on Clara's

37
00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:05.597
shoulder. "Grandfather," he said, "you have given me a gift that can never be

38
00:03:05.598 --> 00:03:11.733
repaid. But if there is any way I can thank you, please let me

39
00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:14.756
know." Grandfather was quiet for a

40
00:03:14.757 --> 00:03:22.547
moment. "I am poor and old," he said, "and I have nothing to leave to Heidi when I

41
00:03:22.548 --> 00:03:33.401
die. If you promise me that Heidi will never have to leave the mountain and earn her living among strangers, then you will be rewarding me

42
00:03:33.402 --> 00:03:36.155
richly." Clara's father did not

43
00:03:36.156 --> 00:03:40.192
hesitate. He said, "I consider Heidi as one of my

44
00:03:40.193 --> 00:03:42.308
family. She will always be looked

45
00:03:42.309 --> 00:03:44.370
after. I promise you

46
00:03:44.371 --> 00:03:51.467
that." Then, Grandmamma realized that Heidi should be rewarded as well for being such a good friend to

47
00:03:51.468 --> 00:03:57.638
Clara. "Heidi, what would you like for your

48
00:03:57.639 --> 00:04:04.138
reward?" Heidi replied immediately, "I would like a warm, beautiful bed for

49
00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:06.706
Grannie. Nothing would please me

50
00:04:06.707 --> 00:04:10.866
more!" Grandmamma happily

51
00:04:10.867 --> 00:04:19.022
agreed. Just then, the sun began to set, and its warm glow shone on the mountaintops in beautiful shades of red and

52
00:04:19.023 --> 00:04:22.611
orange. Heidi felt that her life was truly

53
00:04:22.612 --> 00:04:32.008
blessed. All her friends and family were happy and healthy, and she would never have to leave the mountain

54
